- `fleetctl gitops` now fails, including with `--dry-run`, when the directory part of a `paths:` glob (for example `../platforms/*/reprots/` in `../platforms/*/reprots/*.yml`) matches no existing directory, instead of treating it as an empty list and deleting every existing report, policy, script, label, configuration profile, or app that was defined through it. A glob that matches no files in an existing directory still only logs a warning.
